Subject: Cantor Attention Admission Account Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 79d33f64-2285-4a0d-a09e-c018a6a982f8
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Attention_Admission_Account.sop

& [Problem] is implicit host reasoning at the tool boundary
  + current success proves gates ran but does not serialize their bounded dispositions
  + reconstructing those facts requires controller knowledge and risks confusing Needle proposal with admission

& [Decision] is one deterministic value-private account
  + serialize identities surface field names and gate outcomes only
  + expose the same account to evidence and tool result consumers
  + retain typed faults as the negative account rather than fabricating admission

& [Value] is inspectable attention programming
  + an LLM caller can tell whether it used literal-only delimited or JSON ingress
  + operators can audit which fields were exact-bound without receiving duplicate sensitive content
  + canonical digest supports correlation across evidence and transport

& [Deferred] is signed exterior roots rejected-stage trace envelopes distributed negotiation and semantic-result certification
